{{also|impénétrable}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{q|misspelling}} {{l|en|inpenetrable}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*pen-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|inpenetrabel}}, {{m|enm|inpenetrabyle}}, from {{der|en|frm|impenetrable}} or directly from its etymon, {{der|en|la|impenetrābilis}}.<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary|pos=adj|v=34569}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪmˈpɛnətɹəbəl/|/ɪmˈpɛnɪtɹəbəl/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-impenetrable.wav|a=Southern England}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Usmaan (Middle river exports)-impenetrable.wav|a=UK}}
* {{hyph|en|im|pen|e|tra|ble}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Not [[penetrable]].
#: {{synonyms|en|impregnable}}
#: {{antonyms|en|penetrable|pregnable}}
#: {{ux|en|The fortress is '''impenetrable''', so it cannot be taken.}}
#* {{RQ:NYT|author=John Branch|title=Snow fall: The avalanche at Tunnel Creek|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240611074920/https://www.nytimes.com/projects/2012/snow-fall/index.html|year=2012|passage=The avalanche spread and stopped, locking everything it carried into an icy cocoon. It was now a jagged, virtually '''impenetrable''' pile of ice, longer than a football field and nearly as wide.}}
# [[opaque#English|Opaque]]; [[obscure]]; not [[translucent]] or [[transparent]].
#: {{ux|en|When night falls, she cloaks the world in '''impenetrable''' darkness.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} [[incomprehensible#English|Incomprehensible]]; [[fathomless]]; [[inscrutable]].
#: {{synonyms|en|unfathomable|Thesaurus:incomprehensible}}
#: {{antonyms|en|fathomable|Thesaurus:comprehensible}}
#: {{ux|en|Business jargon makes this document '''impenetrable'''—I can’t understand it.}}

